## 2. Architecture

| Part | Path | Is |
| --- | --- | --- |
| manifest | `domain.json` | the domain's name, summary, request kinds, entry skills, exposure, folders, vault, policy, and unattended level |
| vendored core | `vendor/agent-core/` | the core, which `git subtree` copies from the branch `core` of `agent-core` |
| core units | `.claude/skills/`, `.claude/agents/`, `.claude/workflows/` | a symlink into the vendored core for each core unit the domain uses |
| glossary | `.claude/glossary.md` | the domain's Vocabulary rows and its rules on instruction text |
| audit checks | `audit/checks.py` | the checks the domain adds to the core's audit engine |
| vault config | `obsidian/` | the default Obsidian config, which the folder step copies into the vault's `.obsidian/` |
| user file | `USER.md` | what is true of the user now in this domain; `remember` keeps it |

**The soul file and the user file bind every session.** `CLAUDE.md`
imports this contract, then `vendor/agent-core/SOUL.md`, then `USER.md`. If
a host reads only this contract, read the soul file whole after it. Then
read the user file if it exists.

**The user file is never versioned.** NEVER commit `USER.md`: `.gitignore`
names it, and a test fails if git tracks it.

**The vendored core changes only by `git subtree pull`.** NEVER edit a file
under `vendor/agent-core/`: the next pull overwrites the edit or conflicts
with it. NEVER copy a core unit into `.claude/`: a copy drifts from the
vendored core.

